      "text": "Starting with the given expression \\((2x - 5)(x + 7) - (x + 5)(2x - 1)\\), we will first expand each product separately.\n\n### Expanding \\((2x - 5)(x + 7)\\)\n\nUsing the distributive property (also known as the FOIL method for binomials):\n\n\\[\n(2x - 5)(x + 7) = 2x \\cdot x + 2x \\cdot 7 - 5 \\cdot x - 5 \\cdot 7\n\\]\n\nCalculating each term:\n\n\\[\n2x \\cdot x = 2x^2\n\\]\n\\[\n2x \\cdot 7 = 14x\n\\]\n\\[\n-5 \\cdot x = -5x\n\\]\n\\[\n-5 \\cdot 7 = -35\n\\]\n\nCombine these results:\n\n\\[\n(2x - 5)(x + 7) = 2x^2 + 14x - 5x - 35 = 2x^2 + 9x - 35\n\\]\n\n### Expanding \\((x + 5)(2x - 1)\\)\n\nAgain, using the distributive property:\n\n\\[\n(x + 5)(2x - 1) = x \\cdot 2x + x \\cdot (-1) + 5 \\cdot 2x + 5 \\cdot (-1)\n\\]\n\nCalculating each term:\n\n\\[\nx \\cdot 2x = 2x^2\n\\]\n\\[\nx \\cdot (-1) = -x\n\\]\n\\[\n5 \\cdot 2x = 10x\n\\]\n\\[\n5 \\cdot (-1) = -5\n\\]\n\nCombine these results:\n\n\\[\n(x + 5)(2x - 1) = 2x^2 - x + 10x - 5 = 2x^2 + 9x - 5\n\\]\n\n### Subtracting the two expanded expressions\n\nNow we have:\n\n\\[\n(2x^2 + 9x - 35) - (2x^2 + 9x - 5)\n\\]\n\nDistribute the negative sign through the second expression:\n\n\\[\n2x^2 + 9x - 35 - 2x^2 - 9x + 5\n\\]\n\nCombine like terms:\n\n\\[\n(2x^2 - 2x^2) + (9x - 9x) - 35 + 5\n\\]\n\nSimplify:\n\n\\[\n0 + 0 - 30 = -30\n\\]\n\nThus, the simplified expression is:\n\n\\[\n\\boxed{-30}\n\\]",
